[profiles.guide]
notes = '''This is the gyro variant: tilting the controller moves the cursor, as a fine pointer next to the right stick {rs}. Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller.
The right stick {rs} moves the cursor: {rt} selects (left click, hold to drag a box), and {lt} moves, attacks, takes cover or captures a point (right click). The left stick {ls} scrolls the map, and {up} {down} zoom.
{south} is attack move (then click the target with {rt}), {west} stops and {north} retreats the squad to base. {left} reinforces a squad standing near a building or a reinforcement point, and {right} jumps to the last event. Click {l3} for the next squad in the selection.
Hold {lb} for the control groups and aim the right stick {rs} at one: release to select it. Hold {lb} and {rb} together to put the selection in a group instead (Ctrl + number).
{rb} is Shift: hold it to queue orders or add to the selection. Abilities, items and the wargear are the buttons on the taskbar: click them with {rt}.
Click {r3} for the squad commands, aimed with the right stick {rs}. {select} lists pause, chat and the game menu. Hold {select} for the Menus mode (the main menu, wargear and lobbies) and hold it again to come back. {start} (Esc) is the game menu; {east} cancels.
The keys are the defaults as best known, not checked on an install: reinforce (R) and retreat (T) follow Company of Heroes; stop (S), attack ground (G) and last event (Space) are the likeliest to differ. Keys can be changed only in keydefaults.lua (copy _keydefaults.lua in the settings folder); the grid keys option changes them too. The Linux executable name (DawnOfWar2) is a guess. Guide + {west} opens the on-screen keyboard for chat.'''

